    "reason": "The roman t's bar crosses the stem (330-800, was 430-880) and the 1's flag starts further out, to separate t from r, the pair a reader found hardest (Jandi Mono t/r 0.936 -> 0.916 at 12 px, 0.901 -> 0.849 at 20 px). The cost is t/1 (0.736 -> 0.840 at 20 px) and t/f (about +0.02); the most confusable pair involving t improves at every size in every upright family and is unchanged in the Italic. Bounds: the delta measured locally plus 0.01 for CI's renderer. Accepted by the user.",
